Rule 1 (inputs must be integer or floating-point tensors; no complex)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 3 (if both tensors have a dimension 1, they must match or be singleton to avoid non-broadcastable dim-1 mismatch)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2) then (shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 1) ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 1) = 1)
>>
Rule 4 (out, if provided, must be a tensor)
{v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (out must not have a complex dtype)
{v_3 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 8 (if inputs share the same dtype, out must have that dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) then dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
